export anchor AnimationStudioStyle:
    number: 361
    screen: VideoEditor
    name: Animation studio
    idea: A night animation desk where the viewer sits on a round light table disc with pencil construction lines, panels are punched cel sheets with peg holes, and the timeline is turned upright into an exposure sheet read top to bottom.
    base: dark
    palette:
        nightDesk: #13161d, page, peg holes and the style sheet
        celSheet: #1d2230, punched cel panels and exposure cells
        sheetHead: #232a3b, exposure sheet column heads
        rule: #3a4258, sheet grid and dividers
        lightTable: #2b2a26, the warm disc behind the viewer
        ink: #e3e6ee, text
        graphite: #a5adbf, labels, units and start times
        holdLine: #8b95ad, hold lines running down a clip
        nonPhotoBlue: #8cc0ff, construction lines, the selection, Export and focus
        guideBlue: #4f7fb8, dashed construction guides in the viewer
        redPencil: #ff8f8f, the playhead row rules
        redPencilText: #ffb0b0, playhead and marker notes
    type:
        Headings and notes use a hand stack, Segoe Print, Bradley Hand,
        Chalkboard SE, Comic Neue, Marker Felt. Body is system sans 14px at
        1.5. The timecode and frame numbers use a mono stack, 20px bold and
        13px at 600. Panel titles are hand 20px bold, cel notes hand 19px,
        the pencil test title hand up to 28px bold.
    layout:
        A header holds a ruled slate with Brightwork Cut in blue hand
        lettering and cells Prod Launch teaser, Fmt 1080p and Rate 24 fps,
        then an empty render bar with Render 0% and not inked yet, and a
        blue Export with a pencil icon. The desk is two columns. Every panel
        is a cel sheet with three peg holes punched at the top, one round
        between two oblong. The left column holds Pencil test, the viewer
        set on an oval warm light table disc, the title card with dashed
        blue construction lines behind it, then the timecode, round flip
        buttons with a blue play and the duration. Under it sit two cels,
        Scene folder listing the five files as small punched sheets with
        duration and picture or sound, and Cel notes with Position 960 by
        540, Scale 100 percent, Opacity 100 percent and Cross dissolve 12
        frames handwritten on ruled lines. The right column is the Exposure
        sheet, the timeline turned upright, a table with columns Sec,
        Action, V2 titles, V1 video, A1 voice and A2 music and one row per 6
        seconds from 0 to 90. A clip writes its name and start in the row
        where it begins, a hold line runs down the rows it covers and a
        short rule reads end and the second where it stops. The selected
        title card is in pale blue with a star and a thicker blue hold line.
        The row at 18 is ruled above and below in red pencil with a play
        arrow and playhead 18 in Action, and Action at 84 reads a cross and
        cut to logo. At phone width the folder and notes hide, the Action
        column drops, the 84 row gets a red cross and a handwritten note
        under the sheet explains the marker and playhead.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 24px between cels, 34px top padding to clear the peg holes, 36px sheet rows.
    density: Medium. A sixteen row exposure sheet beside the viewer, folder and notes.
    corners: Cels are 4px at the top and 10px at the bottom. The light table is an oval disc.
    borders: 1px sheet grid, 2px hold lines, 2px red rules round the playhead row.
    shadows: A soft 20px drop under each cel and a faint warm glow around the disc.
    icons: Few and drawn. Peg holes, a star for the selection, a cross for the marker, a play arrow on the playhead row and a pencil on Export.
    focus: A 2px dashed non photo blue outline offset 3px.
    tone: Studio words, such as Pencil test, Scene folder, Cel notes and not inked yet.
